                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p style="text-align: justify;">This course introduces the fundamental theories of dermatology, including the anatomy and functions of the skin, as well as the symptoms and treatment of skin diseases. In conjunction with general principles, it covers the diagnosis, differential diagnosis, and essential prevention and treatment strategies for common and frequently encountered dermatologic and sexually transmitted diseases. These include infectious dermatoses, allergic/immune-mediated skin diseases, drug eruptions, neurofunctional dermatoses, occupational dermatoses, erythematous–scaly diseases, and connective tissue disorders. Through this course, students gain a comprehensive understanding of common dermatologic conditions. Additionally, the course highlights the remarkable contributions and challenging journeys of senior dermatology experts at Shanghai Jiao Tong University and its affiliated hospitals. By integrating ideological and moral education, it aims to convey accurate scientific knowledge while further fostering positive and uplifting values among students.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
